perfcached (0.3.5~rc1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A shape release: the RESP door dispatches from a command table
    instead of a chain of 86 comparisons, and the cluster module reads
    its peer table through one liveness predicate.  No wire, config or
    metric change.
  * Fixed inside this release: a RECOVERING node again refuses DBSIZE,
    FLUSHDB and FLUSHALL with -LOADING.  Putting them behind the table
    had moved them in front of the readiness gate.  No tagged build
    carried it.

