perfcached (0.3.0~rc25-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Collections are created, dropped, resized and renamed while the
    daemon serves, persisted across a restart, carried in the WAL and
    announced to the fleet; the RESP door maps a database index onto a
    collection name, so a Redis-native monitor no longer reports a live
    node as one empty database (S69).  The arena reserves its cap as
    address space and commits by 2 MB group, so every byte up to the cap
    is the same page tier (S97).  The cooperative walk budgets the
    overflow leg instead of draining it whole in its final call (S121).
    Library unchanged (0.2.7).

